      "prompt": "What charged amount is printed by the receipt accessor?\n\n```java\ninterface Payment { int charge(int amount); }\nclass Card implements Payment {\n  public int charge(int amount) { return amount + 5; }\n}\nrecord Receipt(int charged) {}\nPayment payment = new Card();\nReceipt receipt = new Receipt(payment.charge(100));\nSystem.out.println(receipt.charged());\n```",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "5"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "0"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "105"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "100"
        }
      ],
      "correct": [
        "c"
      ],
      "explanation": "payment exposes charge independently of the provider. Card adds the sample provider fee, yielding 105. Receipt stores charged = 105 and exposes charged().",
